# Softmax bearer token for the caos-softmax `tools/gota` tool (Gods of the Arena
# upload + hosted games). https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos-softmax
#
# COMMITTED, and safe to be: neither the token nor its cache-isolation entropy
# is in this file. Both name environment variables, so each user supplies their
# own. Unset, the secret is simply absent and the tool runs anonymous (public
# reads only) and refuses upload/play with a clear message.
#
# To use it, set both in the cloud environment's variables:
#   SOFTMAX_TOKEN               the output of `uv run softmax get-token` after
#                               `uv run softmax login` on your machine. Player
#                               sessions last up to 24h, so refresh it when
#                               `action=status` says unauthenticated.
#   CAOS_SOFTMAX_TOKEN_ENTROPY  any random string of 16+ chars, yours alone
#
# The entropy is what keeps your cached results out of anyone else's reach: it
# is a bearer capability for the cache, so it must not be shared or committed.
name=softmax-token
value:env=SOFTMAX_TOKEN
entropy:env=CAOS_SOFTMAX_TOKEN_ENTROPY

# WHO MAY READ IT: only that tool, at the path it has once imported:
#   import_source(source="https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos-softmax.git",
#                 into="imports/caos-softmax/base")
# A reader naming a path the tree does not carry is dropped with a warning, so
# until the import exists the token reaches nothing.
reader=imports/caos-softmax/base/tools/gota
